  "summary": {
   "status": "complete",
   "text": "In July 2026 testimony, David Rosner said the Commission had acted over the prior year to ensure demand growth leads to a more reliable, affordable, and sustainable grid and that America can win the AI race without regular families paying for it. Rosner encouraged grid operators to deploy automation and artificial intelligence tools shown to accelerate interconnection study steps from years to weeks, saying this in February 2026 as Commissioner and repeating it in July 2026 testimony. Rosner said it is essential to continue deploying 21st-century reliability solutions, including advanced demand response, dynamic line ratings, predictive artificial intelligence, and emerging cybersecurity technologies, in February 2026 as Commissioner and in July 2026 testimony.",
   "sids": [
    "s1",
    "s2",
    "s3",
    "s4",
    "s5"
   ],
